			<item>
				<title>Initial Prep</title>
				<link>https://redzhift.github.io/docs/installation-guide/initial-prep/</link>
				<pubDate>Tue, 23 Jun 2026 15:58:58 -0700</pubDate>
				<guid>https://redzhift.github.io/docs/installation-guide/initial-prep/</guid>
				<description>&lt;div class=&#34;alert alert-success d-flex&#34; role=&#34;alert&#34;&gt;&#xA;  &lt;div class=&#34;flex-shrink-1 alert-icon&#34;&gt;&#xA;  &lt;/div&gt;&#xA;  &lt;div class=&#34;w-100&#34;&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;It is recommended to have:&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;ul&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;USB drive (3.0, at least 8 GB)&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;External HDD or SSD device&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;PC specs (RAM size, GPU model)&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;/div&gt;&#xA;&lt;/div&gt;&#xA;&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;/ul&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;First, back up your files onto an &lt;strong&gt;external HDD/SSD&lt;/strong&gt;. This setup lets you access and recover the files separately if needed.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;h2 id=&#34;download-files&#34;&gt;Download files &lt;a href=&#34;#download-files&#34; class=&#34;anchor&#34; aria-hidden=&#34;true&#34;&gt;&lt;i class=&#34;material-icons align-middle&#34;&gt;link&lt;/i&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;You can download from any mirror listed on the download sites.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;&lt;code&gt;.iso&lt;/code&gt; downloads may take several minutes. Make sure that the download finishes completely before attempting verification.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
			</item>
			<item>
				<title>Verify file integrity</title>
				<link>https://redzhift.github.io/docs/installation-guide/verify-iso/</link>
				<pubDate>Tue, 23 Jun 2026 16:10:36 -0700</pubDate>
				<guid>https://redzhift.github.io/docs/installation-guide/verify-iso/</guid>
				<description>&lt;div class=&#34;alert alert-danger d-flex&#34; role=&#34;alert&#34;&gt;&#xA;  &lt;div class=&#34;flex-shrink-1 alert-icon&#34;&gt;&#xA;  &#xA;  &lt;span class=&#34;material-icons size-20 me-2&#34;&gt;&#xA;  report&#xA;  &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&#xA;  &#xA;  &lt;div class=&#34;w-100&#34;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;You MUST pass this verification step before installation. Otherwise, you run a significant risk of bricking your computer and/or compromising its security.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&#xA;  &lt;/div&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Before using the installation file (&lt;code&gt;.iso&lt;/code&gt;), we need to make sure that it is safe to use. A safe file is:&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;ul&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;From a &lt;strong&gt;verified source&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;Is &lt;strong&gt;not corrupted&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;Has &lt;strong&gt;not been tampered with&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;/ul&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;This verification process is done by comparing &lt;strong&gt;checksums&lt;/strong&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;div class=&#34;alert alert-info d-flex&#34; role=&#34;alert&#34;&gt;&#xA;  &lt;div class=&#34;flex-shrink-1 alert-icon&#34;&gt;&#xA;  &#xA;  &lt;span class=&#34;material-icons size-20 me-2&#34;&gt;&#xA;  info&#xA;  &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&#xA;  &#xA;  &lt;div class=&#34;w-100&#34;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Checksums&lt;/strong&gt;, or hashes, are the &lt;strong&gt;digital fingerprint&lt;/strong&gt; of a file. Any modification or inconsistency creates a different output than the expected hash.&lt;/div&gt;&#xA;  &lt;/div&gt;&#xA;&lt;hr&gt;&#xA;&lt;h2 id=&#34;check-installation-iso-checksum&#34;&gt;Check installation &lt;code&gt;.iso&lt;/code&gt; checksum &lt;a href=&#34;#check-installation-iso-checksum&#34; class=&#34;anchor&#34; aria-hidden=&#34;true&#34;&gt;&lt;i class=&#34;material-icons align-middle&#34;&gt;link&lt;/i&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;Open the &lt;a href=&#34;https://emn178.github.io/online-tools/sha256_checksum.html&#34; rel=&#34;external&#34; target=&#34;_blank&#34;&gt;emn178 SHA256 checksum tool&lt;svg width=&#34;16&#34; height=&#34;16&#34; viewBox=&#34;0 0 24 24&#34; xmlns=&#34;http://www.w3.org/2000/svg&#34;&gt;&lt;path fill=&#34;currentColor&#34; d=&#34;M14 5c-.552 0-1-.448-1-1s.448-1 1-1h6c.552 0 1 .448 1 1v6c0 .552-.448 1-1 1s-1-.448-1-1v-3.586l-7.293 7.293c-.391.39-1.024.39-1.414 0-.391-.391-.391-1.024 0-1.414l7.293-7.293h-3.586zm-9 2c-.552 0-1 .448-1 1v11c0 .552.448 1 1 1h11c.552 0 1-.448 1-1v-4.563c0-.552.448-1 1-1s1 .448 1 1v4.563c0 1.657-1.343 3-3 3h-11c-1.657 0-3-1.343-3-3v-11c0-1.657 1.343-3 3-3h4.563c.552 0 1 .448 1 1s-.448 1-1 1h-4.563z&#34;/&gt;&lt;/svg&gt;&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
			</item>
			<item>
				<title>Create Ventoy Liveboot</title>
				<link>https://redzhift.github.io/docs/installation-guide/create-ventoy-liveboot/</link>
				<pubDate>Tue, 23 Jun 2026 16:10:55 -0700</pubDate>
				<guid>https://redzhift.github.io/docs/installation-guide/create-ventoy-liveboot/</guid>
				<description>&lt;h2 id=&#34;overview&#34;&gt;Overview &lt;a href=&#34;#overview&#34; class=&#34;anchor&#34; aria-hidden=&#34;true&#34;&gt;&lt;i class=&#34;material-icons align-middle&#34;&gt;link&lt;/i&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;A &lt;strong&gt;liveboot USB&lt;/strong&gt; contains a full operating system, which lets you use &amp;rsquo;live session&amp;rsquo; without installing the OS first.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;A &lt;strong&gt;live session&lt;/strong&gt; is required to safely install Linux Mint.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;div class=&#34;alert alert-success d-flex&#34; role=&#34;alert&#34;&gt;&#xA;  &lt;div class=&#34;flex-shrink-1 alert-icon&#34;&gt;&#xA;  &lt;span class=&#34;material-icons size-20 me-2&#34;&gt;&#xA;  check_circle&#xA;  &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&#xA;  &lt;div class=&#34;w-100&#34;&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;In this guide, &lt;strong&gt;Ventoy&lt;/strong&gt; software is used for a more streamlined liveboot experience. This tools lets you select from &lt;strong&gt;multiple boot options&lt;/strong&gt;, so you can install multiple Linux distros to try out on one USB stick.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
			</item>
			<item>
				<title>Install from live session</title>
				<link>https://redzhift.github.io/docs/installation-guide/install-from-live-session/</link>
				<pubDate>Tue, 23 Jun 2026 16:11:03 -0700</pubDate>
				<guid>https://redzhift.github.io/docs/installation-guide/install-from-live-session/</guid>
				<description>&lt;h2 id=&#34;overview&#34;&gt;Overview &lt;a href=&#34;#overview&#34; class=&#34;anchor&#34; aria-hidden=&#34;true&#34;&gt;&lt;i class=&#34;material-icons align-middle&#34;&gt;link&lt;/i&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;With your &lt;strong&gt;liveboot USB&lt;/strong&gt; set up, you can prepare to boot into a &lt;strong&gt;live session&lt;/strong&gt; of Linux Mint.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;First, you need to set your computer system to recognize that it should boot from a different device at startup (your &lt;strong&gt;Ventoy&lt;/strong&gt; device). This option is changed in your computer’s &lt;code&gt;BIOS MENU&lt;/code&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;hr&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;nav&gt;&#xA;&#x9;&lt;div class=&#34;nav nav-tabs&#34; id=&#34;nav-tab&#34; role=&#34;tablist&#34;&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&#x9;&#x9;&#xA;&#x9;&#x9;&#xA;&#x9;&#x9;&#xA;&#x9;&#x9;&#xA;&#xA;&#x9;&#x9;&#xA;&#xA;&#x9;&#x9;&lt;a class=&#34;nav-link  active&#34;&#xA;&#x9;&#x9;   id=&#34;aefbcdTab&#34; data-bs-toggle=&#34;tab&#34; data-bs-target=&#34;#aefbcd&#34;&#xA;&#x9;&#x9;   type=&#34;button&#34; role=&#34;tab&#34; aria-controls=&#34;aefbcd&#34; aria-selected=&#34;true&#34;&gt;Disable secure boot in BIOS&lt;/a&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&#x9;&#x9;&#xA;&#xA;&#x9;&#x9;&lt;a class=&#34;nav-link &#34;&#xA;&#x9;&#x9;   id=&#34;edcafbTab&#34; data-bs-toggle=&#34;tab&#34; data-bs-target=&#34;#edcafb&#34;&#xA;&#x9;&#x9;   type=&#34;button&#34; role=&#34;tab&#34; aria-controls=&#34;edcafb&#34; aria-selected=&#34;true&#34;&gt;Change default boot order&lt;/a&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&#x9;&#x9;&#xA;&#xA;&#x9;&lt;/div&gt;&#xA;&lt;/nav&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;div class=&#34;tab-content&#34; id=&#34;nav-tab-content&#34;&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&#x9;&#xA;&#xA;&#xA;&#xA;&#xA;&#xA;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;div class=&#34;tab-pane fade show active&#34; id=&#34;aefbcd&#34; role=&#34;tabpanel&#34; aria-labelledby=&#34;nav-1&#34;&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&#x9;&lt;h2 id=&#34;disable-secure-boot-in-bios-menu&#34;&gt;Disable secure boot in &lt;code&gt;BIOS MENU&lt;/code&gt; &lt;a href=&#34;#disable-secure-boot-in-bios-menu&#34; class=&#34;anchor&#34; aria-hidden=&#34;true&#34;&gt;&lt;i class=&#34;material-icons align-middle&#34;&gt;link&lt;/i&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;ol&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Reboot your computer with the &lt;strong&gt;Ventoy USB&lt;/strong&gt; still inserted.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
			</item>
			<item>
				<title>Change default kernel</title>
				<link>https://redzhift.github.io/docs/user-guides/user-config/change-default-kernel/</link>
				<pubDate>Mon, 08 Jun 2026 16:58:36 -0700</pubDate>
				<guid>https://redzhift.github.io/docs/user-guides/user-config/change-default-kernel/</guid>
				<description>&lt;hr&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;div class=&#34;alert alert-info d-flex&#34; role=&#34;alert&#34;&gt;&#xA;  &lt;div class=&#34;flex-shrink-1 alert-icon&#34;&gt;&#xA;  &#xA;  &lt;span class=&#34;material-icons size-20 me-2&#34;&gt;&#xA;  info&#xA;  &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&#xA;  &#xA;  &lt;div class=&#34;w-100&#34;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Note&lt;/strong&gt;: This guide is for systems using the default &lt;code&gt;systemd-boot&lt;/code&gt; UEFI boot manager in Endeavour OS.&lt;/div&gt;&#xA;  &lt;/div&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Your system can have multiple kernels (or versions) of Linux. The default kernel is usually set to the newest one, but can be adjusted to user preference.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;First, you need to identify and adjust the kernel &lt;code&gt;ids&lt;/code&gt; used in the &lt;code&gt;boot loader&lt;/code&gt; config file.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;hr&gt;&#xA;&lt;h3 id=&#34;find-the-kernel-id&#34;&gt;Find the kernel &lt;code&gt;id&lt;/code&gt; &lt;a href=&#34;#find-the-kernel-id&#34; class=&#34;anchor&#34; aria-hidden=&#34;true&#34;&gt;&lt;i class=&#34;material-icons align-middle&#34;&gt;link&lt;/i&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;&#xA;&lt;nav&gt;&#xA;&#x9;&lt;div class=&#34;nav nav-tabs&#34; id=&#34;nav-tab&#34; role=&#34;tablist&#34;&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&#x9;&#x9;&#xA;&#x9;&#x9;&#xA;&#x9;&#x9;&#xA;&#x9;&#x9;&#xA;&#xA;&#x9;&#x9;&#xA;&#xA;&#x9;&#x9;&lt;a class=&#34;nav-link  active&#34;&#xA;&#x9;&#x9;   id=&#34;dbecafTab&#34; data-bs-toggle=&#34;tab&#34; data-bs-target=&#34;#dbecaf&#34;&#xA;&#x9;&#x9;   type=&#34;button&#34; role=&#34;tab&#34; aria-controls=&#34;dbecaf&#34; aria-selected=&#34;true&#34;&gt;Use `bootctl` to view kernel info&lt;/a&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&#x9;&#x9;&#xA;&#xA;&#x9;&#x9;&lt;a class=&#34;nav-link &#34;&#xA;&#x9;&#x9;   id=&#34;dfbaceTab&#34; data-bs-toggle=&#34;tab&#34; data-bs-target=&#34;#dfbace&#34;&#xA;&#x9;&#x9;   type=&#34;button&#34; role=&#34;tab&#34; aria-controls=&#34;dfbace&#34; aria-selected=&#34;true&#34;&gt;Use `cat` to view current default&lt;/a&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&#x9;&#x9;&#xA;&#xA;&#x9;&lt;/div&gt;&#xA;&lt;/nav&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;div class=&#34;tab-content&#34; id=&#34;nav-tab-content&#34;&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&#x9;&#xA;&#xA;&#xA;&#xA;&#xA;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;div class=&#34;tab-pane fade show active&#34; id=&#34;dbecaf&#34; role=&#34;tabpanel&#34; aria-labelledby=&#34;nav-1&#34;&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&#x9;&lt;h4 id=&#34;find-kernel-id-with-bootctl&#34;&gt;Find kernel &lt;code&gt;id&lt;/code&gt; with &lt;code&gt;bootctl&lt;/code&gt; &lt;a href=&#34;#find-kernel-id-with-bootctl&#34; class=&#34;anchor&#34; aria-hidden=&#34;true&#34;&gt;&lt;i class=&#34;material-icons align-middle&#34;&gt;link&lt;/i&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;ol&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Change to the root user with &lt;code&gt;sudo -s&lt;/code&gt; and enter your password.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
			</item>
			<item>
				<title>Downgrade with eos-shifttime</title>
				<link>https://redzhift.github.io/docs/user-guides/user-config/downgrade-to-specific-date/</link>
				<pubDate>Wed, 13 May 2026 14:09:31 -0700</pubDate>
				<guid>https://redzhift.github.io/docs/user-guides/user-config/downgrade-to-specific-date/</guid>
				<description>&lt;hr&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;div class=&#34;alert alert-warning d-flex&#34; role=&#34;alert&#34;&gt;&#xA;  &lt;div class=&#34;flex-shrink-1 alert-icon&#34;&gt;&#xA;  &#xA;  &lt;span class=&#34;material-icons size-20 me-2&#34;&gt;&#xA;  warning&#xA;  &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&#xA;  &#xA;  &lt;div class=&#34;w-100&#34;&gt;Using &lt;code&gt;eos-shifttime&lt;/code&gt; does not revert AUR packages. The downgrade only applies to official Arch packages from the archive repositories.&lt;/div&gt;&#xA;  &lt;/div&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;The &lt;code&gt;eos-shifttime&lt;/code&gt; application can revert system packages to their state at a specified date.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;ol&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Open a terminal window and run &lt;code&gt;eos-shifttime&lt;/code&gt; with root permissions.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Select the date to revert to on the GUI window, then click &lt;strong&gt;Revert&lt;/strong&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Reboot&lt;/strong&gt; to apply the changes.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;/ol&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&#xA;&#xA;&#xA;&#xA;  &#xA;&#xA;&#xA;&#xA;  &#xA;    &#xA;      &lt;img src=&#34;https://redzhift.github.io/images/eos-shifttime.png&#34; alt=&#34;A GUI window for the eos-shifttime tool displaying a monthly calendar. The selected date is January 2, 2026.&#34; width=&#34;652&#34; height=&#34;543&#34; loading=&#34;lazy&#34;&gt;&#xA;    &#xA;  &#xA;&lt;/p&gt;</description>
			</item>
			<item>
				<title>Install new theme in Typora</title>
				<link>https://redzhift.github.io/docs/user-guides/user-config/install-new-theme-in-typora/</link>
				<pubDate>Thu, 25 Jun 2026 10:37:17 -0700</pubDate>
				<guid>https://redzhift.github.io/docs/user-guides/user-config/install-new-theme-in-typora/</guid>
				<description>&lt;hr&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;&lt;br&gt;&#xA;&lt;strong&gt;Typora&lt;/strong&gt; is a minimalist text editor that renders markdown and code in real-time. The software comes with several default themes that can be applied through the &lt;strong&gt;Themes&lt;/strong&gt; option menu.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;First, find which custom theme you&amp;rsquo;d like to install from the &lt;a href=&#34;https://theme.typora.io/&#34; rel=&#34;external&#34; target=&#34;_blank&#34;&gt;Typora themes page&lt;svg width=&#34;16&#34; height=&#34;16&#34; viewBox=&#34;0 0 24 24&#34; xmlns=&#34;http://www.w3.org/2000/svg&#34;&gt;&lt;path fill=&#34;currentColor&#34; d=&#34;M14 5c-.552 0-1-.448-1-1s.448-1 1-1h6c.552 0 1 .448 1 1v6c0 .552-.448 1-1 1s-1-.448-1-1v-3.586l-7.293 7.293c-.391.39-1.024.39-1.414 0-.391-.391-.391-1.024 0-1.414l7.293-7.293h-3.586zm-9 2c-.552 0-1 .448-1 1v11c0 .552.448 1 1 1h11c.552 0 1-.448 1-1v-4.563c0-.552.448-1 1-1s1 .448 1 1v4.563c0 1.657-1.343 3-3 3h-11c-1.657 0-3-1.343-3-3v-11c0-1.657 1.343-3 3-3h4.563c.552 0 1 .448 1 1s-.448 1-1 1h-4.563z&#34;/&gt;&lt;/svg&gt;&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
			</item>
			<item>
				<title>Linux Mint Installation</title>
				<link>https://redzhift.github.io/docs/installation-guide/</link>
				<pubDate>Tue, 23 Jun 2026 15:54:19 -0700</pubDate>
				<guid>https://redzhift.github.io/docs/installation-guide/</guid>
				<description></description>
			</item>
			<item>
				<title>Update packages</title>
				<link>https://redzhift.github.io/docs/user-guides/system-maintenance/update-packages/</link>
				<pubDate>Tue, 12 May 2026 14:09:31 -0700</pubDate>
				<guid>https://redzhift.github.io/docs/user-guides/system-maintenance/update-packages/</guid>
				<description>&lt;p&gt;There are 3 commands used to update &lt;strong&gt;Endeavour OS&lt;/strong&gt; systems:&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;nav&gt;&#xA;&#x9;&lt;div class=&#34;nav nav-tabs&#34; id=&#34;nav-tab&#34; role=&#34;tablist&#34;&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&#x9;&#x9;&#xA;&#x9;&#x9;&#xA;&#x9;&#x9;&#xA;&#x9;&#x9;&#xA;&#xA;&#x9;&#x9;&#xA;&#xA;&#x9;&#x9;&lt;a class=&#34;nav-link  active&#34;&#xA;&#x9;&#x9;   id=&#34;bfaecdTab&#34; data-bs-toggle=&#34;tab&#34; data-bs-target=&#34;#bfaecd&#34;&#xA;&#x9;&#x9;   type=&#34;button&#34; role=&#34;tab&#34; aria-controls=&#34;bfaecd&#34; aria-selected=&#34;true&#34;&gt;pacman -Syu&lt;/a&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&#x9;&#x9;&#xA;&#xA;&#x9;&#x9;&lt;a class=&#34;nav-link &#34;&#xA;&#x9;&#x9;   id=&#34;dcabefTab&#34; data-bs-toggle=&#34;tab&#34; data-bs-target=&#34;#dcabef&#34;&#xA;&#x9;&#x9;   type=&#34;button&#34; role=&#34;tab&#34; aria-controls=&#34;dcabef&#34; aria-selected=&#34;true&#34;&gt;yay&lt;/a&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&#x9;&#x9;&#xA;&#xA;&#x9;&#x9;&lt;a class=&#34;nav-link &#34;&#xA;&#x9;&#x9;   id=&#34;ebfcadTab&#34; data-bs-toggle=&#34;tab&#34; data-bs-target=&#34;#ebfcad&#34;&#xA;&#x9;&#x9;   type=&#34;button&#34; role=&#34;tab&#34; aria-controls=&#34;ebfcad&#34; aria-selected=&#34;true&#34;&gt;eos-update&lt;/a&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&#x9;&#x9;&#xA;&#xA;&#x9;&lt;/div&gt;&#xA;&lt;/nav&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;div class=&#34;tab-content&#34; id=&#34;nav-tab-content&#34;&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&#x9;&#xA;&#xA;&#xA;&#xA;&#xA;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;div class=&#34;tab-pane fade show active&#34; id=&#34;bfaecd&#34; role=&#34;tabpanel&#34; aria-labelledby=&#34;nav-1&#34;&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&#x9;&lt;p&gt;&lt;code&gt;pacman&lt;/code&gt; is the package manager used to install and update programs in Arch Linux.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;To perform a full system update and refresh, run:&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&#xA;&#xA;  &#xA;  &#xA;  &#xA;&#xA;  &#xA;  &#xA;  &#xA;  &#xA;&#xA;  &#xA;&#xA;  &lt;div class=&#34;prism-codeblock &#34;&gt;&#xA;  &lt;pre id=&#34;902b365&#34; class=&#34;language-sh &#34;&gt;&#xA;  &lt;code&gt;$ sudo pacman -Syu&lt;/code&gt;&#xA;  &lt;/pre&gt;&#xA;  &lt;/div&gt;&#xA;&lt;div class=&#34;alert alert-info d-flex&#34; role=&#34;alert&#34;&gt;&#xA;  &lt;div class=&#34;flex-shrink-1 alert-icon&#34;&gt;&#xA;  &lt;span class=&#34;material-icons size-20 me-2&#34;&gt;&#xA;  info&#xA;  &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&#xA;  &lt;div class=&#34;w-100&#34;&gt;Some commands require prepending &lt;code&gt;sudo&lt;/code&gt; to them as they require &lt;code&gt;super user&lt;/code&gt; (or root) permissions to run.&lt;/div&gt;&#xA;  &lt;/div&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Example terminal output&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</description>
			</item>
			<item>
				<title>Re-rank mirrors</title>
				<link>https://redzhift.github.io/docs/user-guides/system-maintenance/rerank-mirrors/</link>
				<pubDate>Fri, 12 Jun 2026 18:00:22 -0700</pubDate>
				<guid>https://redzhift.github.io/docs/user-guides/system-maintenance/rerank-mirrors/</guid>
				<description>&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Mirrors&lt;/strong&gt; are servers located around the world that store copies of software packages. When upgrading packages, your EndeavourOS system utilizes multiple mirrors, which are noted in a &lt;code&gt;mirrorlist&lt;/code&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;A well-maintained &lt;code&gt;mirrorlist&lt;/code&gt; ensures the &lt;code&gt;pacman&lt;/code&gt; package manager can access up-to-date package files when performing system updates. Outdated mirrors can prevent &lt;code&gt;pacman&lt;/code&gt; from updating &lt;strong&gt;core packages&lt;/strong&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;hr&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;nav&gt;&#xA;&#x9;&lt;div class=&#34;nav nav-tabs&#34; id=&#34;nav-tab&#34; role=&#34;tablist&#34;&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&#x9;&#x9;&#xA;&#x9;&#x9;&#xA;&#x9;&#x9;&#xA;&#x9;&#x9;&#xA;&#xA;&#x9;&#x9;&#xA;&#xA;&#x9;&#x9;&lt;a class=&#34;nav-link  active&#34;&#xA;&#x9;&#x9;   id=&#34;abfcedTab&#34; data-bs-toggle=&#34;tab&#34; data-bs-target=&#34;#abfced&#34;&#xA;&#x9;&#x9;   type=&#34;button&#34; role=&#34;tab&#34; aria-controls=&#34;abfced&#34; aria-selected=&#34;true&#34;&gt;Re-rank Arch mirrors&lt;/a&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&#x9;&#x9;&#xA;&#xA;&#x9;&#x9;&lt;a class=&#34;nav-link &#34;&#xA;&#x9;&#x9;   id=&#34;dbcefaTab&#34; data-bs-toggle=&#34;tab&#34; data-bs-target=&#34;#dbcefa&#34;&#xA;&#x9;&#x9;   type=&#34;button&#34; role=&#34;tab&#34; aria-controls=&#34;dbcefa&#34; aria-selected=&#34;true&#34;&gt;Re-rank EndeavourOS mirrors&lt;/a&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&#x9;&#x9;&#xA;&#xA;&#x9;&#x9;&lt;a class=&#34;nav-link &#34;&#xA;&#x9;&#x9;   id=&#34;aebfdcTab&#34; data-bs-toggle=&#34;tab&#34; data-bs-target=&#34;#aebfdc&#34;&#xA;&#x9;&#x9;   type=&#34;button&#34; role=&#34;tab&#34; aria-controls=&#34;aebfdc&#34; aria-selected=&#34;true&#34;&gt;Common issues&lt;/a&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&#x9;&#x9;&#xA;&#xA;&#x9;&lt;/div&gt;&#xA;&lt;/nav&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;div class=&#34;tab-content&#34; id=&#34;nav-tab-content&#34;&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&#x9;&#xA;&#xA;&#xA;&#xA;&#xA;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;div class=&#34;tab-pane fade show active&#34; id=&#34;abfced&#34; role=&#34;tabpanel&#34; aria-labelledby=&#34;nav-1&#34;&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&#x9;&lt;p&gt;Update the Arch &lt;code&gt;mirrorlist&lt;/code&gt; by running:&lt;/p&gt;</description>
			</item>
			<item>
				<title>Why do I get errors when I try to update?</title>
				<link>https://redzhift.github.io/docs/user-guides/faqs/getting-update-errors/</link>
				<pubDate>Fri, 12 Jun 2026 18:00:22 -0700</pubDate>
				<guid>https://redzhift.github.io/docs/user-guides/faqs/getting-update-errors/</guid>
				<description>&lt;p&gt;Outdated package databases will cause errors when &lt;code&gt;pacman&lt;/code&gt; tries to retrieve the latest package files.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;This can be prevented through regular mirror maintenance.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;See: &lt;a href=&#34;https://redzhift.github.io/docs/user-guides/system-maintenance/rerank-mirrors/&#34;&gt;Update mirrors guide&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;hr&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Error: failed to commit transaction (conflicting files)&lt;/strong&gt;:&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Running a &lt;code&gt;sudo pacman -Syu&lt;/code&gt; update may fail and display the following errors:&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&#xA;&#xA;  &#xA;  &#xA;  &#xA;&#xA;  &#xA;  &#xA;  &#xA;  &#xA;&#xA;  &#xA;&#xA;  &lt;div class=&#34;prism-codeblock &#34;&gt;&#xA;  &lt;pre id=&#34;2af6cbd&#34; class=&#34;language-sh &#34;&gt;&#xA;  &lt;code&gt; error: failed to commit transaction (conflicting files)&#xA; &amp;lt;example&amp;gt;: /example exists in filesystem (owned by filesystem)&#xA; &amp;lt;example&amp;gt;: /lib/systemd/system/example.service exists in filesystem&lt;/code&gt;&#xA;  &lt;/pre&gt;&#xA;  &lt;/div&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;These issues can be resolved with manual intervention. Uninstall and remove the package from the system, then reinstall/update with these two commands:&lt;/p&gt;</description>
			</item>
			<item>
				<title>Are there mirror management alternatives?</title>
				<link>https://redzhift.github.io/docs/user-guides/faqs/mirror-alternatives/</link>
				<pubDate>Fri, 12 Jun 2026 18:00:22 -0700</pubDate>
				<guid>https://redzhift.github.io/docs/user-guides/faqs/mirror-alternatives/</guid>
				<description>&lt;p&gt;Popular alternatives to mirror management are listed on the &lt;a href=&#34;https://wiki.archlinux.org/title/Mirrors&#34; rel=&#34;external&#34; target=&#34;_blank&#34;&gt;Arch mirrors wiki&lt;svg width=&#34;16&#34; height=&#34;16&#34; viewBox=&#34;0 0 24 24&#34; xmlns=&#34;http://www.w3.org/2000/svg&#34;&gt;&lt;path fill=&#34;currentColor&#34; d=&#34;M14 5c-.552 0-1-.448-1-1s.448-1 1-1h6c.552 0 1 .448 1 1v6c0 .552-.448 1-1 1s-1-.448-1-1v-3.586l-7.293 7.293c-.391.39-1.024.39-1.414 0-.391-.391-.391-1.024 0-1.414l7.293-7.293h-3.586zm-9 2c-.552 0-1 .448-1 1v11c0 .552.448 1 1 1h11c.552 0 1-.448 1-1v-4.563c0-.552.448-1 1-1s1 .448 1 1v4.563c0 1.657-1.343 3-3 3h-11c-1.657 0-3-1.343-3-3v-11c0-1.657 1.343-3 3-3h4.563c.552 0 1 .448 1 1s-.448 1-1 1h-4.563z&#34;/&gt;&lt;/svg&gt;&lt;/a&gt;. Some programs can automate mirror management when configured properly.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;One such example is &lt;code&gt;ghostmirror&lt;/code&gt;, which:&lt;/p&gt;</description>
			</item>
			<item>
				<title>What is the AUR?</title>
				<link>https://redzhift.github.io/docs/user-guides/faqs/what-is-aur/</link>
				<pubDate>Fri, 12 Jun 2026 18:00:22 -0700</pubDate>
				<guid>https://redzhift.github.io/docs/user-guides/faqs/what-is-aur/</guid>
				<description>&lt;p&gt;The &lt;strong&gt;Arch User Repository&lt;/strong&gt; (known as &lt;strong&gt;AUR&lt;/strong&gt;) is a large library of community user-produced packages for Arch Linux.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Popular and well-maintained packages are voted on by the community to include in the official Arch &lt;code&gt;extra&lt;/code&gt; repository.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;hr&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;To download and install AUR packages&lt;/strong&gt;:&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;ol&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Clone the &lt;code&gt;git&lt;/code&gt; repository listed on the package&amp;rsquo;s AUR page:&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&#xA;&#xA;  &#xA;  &#xA;  &#xA;&#xA;  &#xA;  &#xA;  &#xA;  &#xA;&#xA;  &#xA;&#xA;  &lt;div class=&#34;prism-codeblock &#34;&gt;&#xA;  &lt;pre id=&#34;6a1139a&#34; class=&#34;language-sh &#34;&gt;&#xA;  &lt;code&gt; git clone https://aur.archlinux.org/&amp;lt;pkg&amp;gt;.git&lt;/code&gt;&#xA;  &lt;/pre&gt;&#xA;  &lt;/div&gt;&#xA;&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Change into the package directory:&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&#xA;&#xA;  &#xA;  &#xA;  &#xA;&#xA;  &#xA;  &#xA;  &#xA;  &#xA;&#xA;  &#xA;&#xA;  &lt;div class=&#34;prism-codeblock &#34;&gt;&#xA;  &lt;pre id=&#34;979430f&#34; class=&#34;language-sh &#34;&gt;&#xA;  &lt;code&gt;cd &amp;lt;pkg&amp;gt;&lt;/code&gt;&#xA;  &lt;/pre&gt;&#xA;  &lt;/div&gt;&#xA;&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Build and install the package with:&lt;/p&gt;</description>
			</item>
